    {
      "Text": "An update for openssh is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An open source implementation of SSH protocol version 2\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nssh in OpenSSH before 10.4 can have a use-after-free when a server changes its host key during a key re-exchange. (This outcome occurs only on the client side.)(CVE-2026-60002)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for openssh is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of critical. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
